<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/nist-rmf> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "NIST AI Risk Management Framework 1.0 — function mapping"@en ;
    dct:description "OWL + SHACL projection of the Interego substrate's NIST AI RMF mapping (https://markjspivey-xwisee.github.io/interego/ns/nist-rmf): the four core functions (Govern / Map / Measure / Manage), so that a record of an action can name the function it contributes to. Composed into PGSL and projected here so a cited function IRI dereferences."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by NIST. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "AI RMF 1.0 is the current version of the framework; NIST's later publications, such as the Generative AI Profile (NIST AI 600-1, 2024), are profiles of it and keep its four functions."@en ,
        "Mapped to the Interego substrate's NIST AI RMF vocabulary (prefix nist-rmf:, https://markjspivey-xwisee.github.io/interego/ns/nist-rmf) by SKOS mappings."@en ,
        "The four functions are the concepts of one list (CoreFunction). Each is a Function, typed with its own class (Govern, Map, Measure, Manage), and carries its id: the class, the list and the id name the same four functions, and a record that names a CoreFunction concept meets the function shape."@en ,
        "An instance written as JSON is read into this ontology through the JSON-LD 1.1 context published at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/nist-rmf/context/2026.10.1, which is generated from this document. The shapes at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/nist-rmf/shapes/2026.10.1 constrain that reading, and the Foxxi validator (POST https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/nist-rmf/validate) checks the JSON against the same shapes."@en ,
        "The shapes select a node by its class (sh:targetClass) and, as the RDFS domain and range rules make a node an instance of a class, by a property it has (sh:targetSubjectsOf) or by the property that reaches it (sh:targetObjectsOf): a node is checked whether or not it declares its type. The Foxxi validator selects the same nodes of the JSON, and every result cites its shape."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/nist-rmf#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/nist-rmf/2026.10.1> ;
